# tally 2.1.8 S7 (#174), L §7.6 Limits 6: one line's windows each takes at most 20 000 combinations of days (RUN-LIMIT,
# L §8.4's form `windows each over more than 20 000 day combinations`). wide's window holds 20 089 days: late is refused,
# the line alone; few takes narrow's three days in two runs, and plain is the imprecise hole. 2.1.7's refcore stopped
# REFCORE-NOT-YET; the engine prints RUN-LIMIT.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input wide: date
input narrow: date

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  wide = window(2026-01-01, 2080-12-31) "s"
  narrow = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-03) "s"

ask late: wide > 2026-03-01 windows each
ask few: narrow > 2026-03-01 windows each
ask plain: wide > 2026-03-01
=== expect
few [narrow = 2026-03-01]: false
  cut 2026-06-30
few [narrow = 2026-03-02 .. 2026-03-03]: true
  cut 2026-06-30
late: refused: RUN-LIMIT windows each over more than 20 000 day combinations
plain: ?"date within window(2026-01-01, 2080-12-31) not precise enough for wide > 2026-03-01" (wide)
  cut 2026-06-30
